# MySQL Workbench model. A zip archive — never let git treat it as text: a line-ending
# rewrite or an auto-merge corrupts the file silently, and Workbench then refuses to open
# it. Binary also means conflicts surface as "take mine / take theirs", which is the only
# sane resolution for a model nobody can merge by hand.
*.mwb binary

# Shell scripts keep LF line endings in the working copy too. With core.autocrlf=true
# Windows checks them out as CRLF, and if the folder is copied to the Linux server,
# bash fails with `bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M` (the nightly backup scripts would just
# stop running).
*.sh text eol=lf
